# Style
PEP 8, line length 88, type hints on public functions. f-strings are fine. Never use them for SQL or shell.

# Flask in this repo
- Console MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH is 256 KiB. Worker job body is 64 KiB. Do not raise either without a reason.
- DEBUG stays off outside development. Production requires COOKIE_SECURE=1. Do not infer HTTPS from X-Forwarded-Proto.
- Every /api route except the existing public list (login, guest, health on the worker) needs a session and an authorization check. Check ownership, not only the role.
- Validate JSON by reading known fields. Ignore unknown fields. Do not mass-assign request.json onto a row.
- Login rate limit already lives in the database. Reuse that pattern. Do not add Flask-Limiter unless asked.
- Compare secrets with hmac.compare_digest or the existing same_secret helper. Randomness uses secrets, not random.
- Outbound calls need a timeout. subprocess uses a list, shell=False, and a timeout.
- Return a short error string. Do not return tracebacks.
